==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|solh₂}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fro|salutacion}}, from {{der|en|la|salutatio||a greeting, a wishing health to}}, from {{m|la|saluto||wish one’s health, greet}}, from {{m|la|salus||well-being}}. Compare the Latin greeting ''[[salvere|salve]]'' (“be well”).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# A [[greeting]], [[salute]], or [[address]]; a [[hello]].
# The act of greeting.
#* {{RQ:Critical Pronouncing Dictionary|page=571|passage={{smallcaps|Welcome}}, we²l'ku²m. a.<br> Received with gladneſs, admitted willingly, grateful{{...}}<br>{{smallcaps|Welcome}}, we²l'ku²m. interj.<br> A form of '''ſalutation''' uſed to a new comer.|ppage=1}}
# The title in a person's name, such as [[Mr]], [[Mrs]], [[Ms.]], [[Dr.]], or [[Rev.]]
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Quickening; excitement.

